@startuml agent-authoring
' ============================================================================
'  How an agent persists a SKILL / SCRIPT / RESOURCE - always via a tool call.
'  Render: java -jar ../../../plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng agent-authoring.puml
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #888888
skinparam ArrowFontColor #5A5A5A
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam activityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam activityDiamondBorderColor #C9B458
skinparam activityBorderColor #999999
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam noteBorderColor #C9B458

title How an agent writes a skill / script / resource - it is ALWAYS a tool call

start

#E1F5FE:**Engine loop** - the model decides to persist something
and EMITS A TOOL CALL (nothing is written by magic);
#E8F5E9:**GuardedTool** chokepoint
(timeout / retry / error-norm / policy + approval = seam);

if (what is it persisting?) then (a reusable PROCEDURE = know-how)
  #C8E6C9:**skill_workshop** (create / update);
  #C8E6C9:writes  skills/NAME/SKILL.md  (immediately, no approval today);
  #FFF8E1:advertised in the prompt NEXT turn,
  read on demand with the read tool;
elseif (a raw FILE / SCRIPT / OUTPUT) then (file)
  #C8E6C9:**write**(path, content)   or   **edit**;
  #C8E6C9:writes  workspace/PATH  (relative paths root at the workspace);
  #FFF8E1:resource RECONCILE next turn scans the workspace,
  basic-describes it + indexes into resources.sqlite;
else (a managed RESOURCE = described + indexed)
  #C8E6C9:**resource** create / edit / delete;
  #C8E6C9:writes workspace/PATH
  + updates resources.sqlite (cached, described)
  + enqueue_enrich -> BACKGROUND (vision / LLM summary);
  #FFF8E1:in the index immediately - manifest shows it next turn;
endif

stop

legend bottom
  EVERYTHING the agent persists is a TOOL CALL inside the engine loop: the model picks the tool,
  the tool writes to disk, and the result is surfaced back next turn - a skill ADVERTISED, or a file /
  resource listed in the workspace-resources MANIFEST. (write-tool files are indexed lazily by the next
  reconcile; the resource tool indexes immediately + enriches in the background.)
  --
  Resource timing detail: resource-flow.puml.    The whole turn: agent-full-flow.puml.
endlegend

@enduml
